---
term: Member
aka:
  - Membership
section: building-blocks
order: 40
definition: A person or corporation that belongs to a corporation and holds the rights and obligations its charter defines.
seeAlso:
  - exit
  - representation-vector
  - ownership
  - status
---
In a democratic charter, members hold [[constitutional authority]]. They control how the charter evolves, while executives carry it out. Whether members hold that authority is a choice for each charter's design. Membership rights are distinct from property rights and from delegated public authority.

Member is one of five [[status|statuses]] that a charter can hold toward a party. A party that holds a [[contract]] with the charter instead of membership is an [[associate]].
